Z||000000||Leadfoot||07-25-2001||04:09 PM||||Not long ago I installed a fresh 2.8L.  Right now it has about 800 miles on it.  I have been running 5w30 since day one.  Every time I start up the engine the oil pressure gauge pegs out (even at idle).  Eventually as the car warms up the oil pressure seems to be correct (30-75 psi from idle to 4k).  Is it possible that the oil sensor is bad?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||07-25-2001||04:12 PM||||That sounds about right.<BR>If you want to double check for accuracy, put a manual gauge on to check with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||07-25-2001||06:23 PM||||When the oil sender goes completely, the guage will stay pegged when the car is running.  Sort of a pain in the but to replace...no room to work unless you remove the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000003||b lo 0||07-26-2001||02:17 PM||||replace the sensor NOW to be sure it doesn't screw up anything else!||||reg||1
